-- `l4 batch` prints the checked module back and checks it again next to a
-- generated record that has a field for each input. The printer writes this
-- annotation back, so `%a%` could have two candidates, the input and the
-- field; if the checker refused that ("multiple definitions"), every row would
-- be an `error`. The row runs.

@export Whether the amount is large
GIVEN a IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is large` @nlg the amount %a% is large
  IF a GREATER THAN 100
